🔐 STIG Remediation: Restrict 'Back up files and directories' User Right

STIG ID: WN11-UR-000030
Severity: Medium
Vulnerability Status: ⚠️ Deprecated Audit — May be removed in a future update

📖 Overview

This STIG ensures that only authorized users — specifically the Administrators group — have the Back up files and directories user right. Misconfigured privileges can lead to unauthorized access to sensitive data by bypassing standard file and folder permissions.

⚠️ Why It Matters

Accounts with the Back up files and directories right can circumvent NTFS file system permissions, potentially accessing or exfiltrating sensitive data. Limiting this capability is essential for reducing insider threat risk or lateral movement by threat actors.

🔍 Check: User Rights Assignment

Open the Local Security Policy tool (secpol.msc).
Navigate to:

```
Computer Configuration >>
Windows Settings >>
Security Settings >>
Local Policies >>
User Rights Assignment
```

Locate the policy:
Back up files and directories
Verify it only includes:
Administrators
❌ If any other groups or users are listed (e.g., Backup Operators, Users), this is a finding.

📎 Notes

The Backup Operators group is often added by default in some systems — remove it unless explicitly required and documented.
Because this audit is marked deprecated, it may no longer be supported in future STIG releases, but it remains a valid best practice for securing privilege escalation vectors.
